FILE: vUX-formComponents.js
FEATURE: component-teardown
DATE: 2026-09-17
PRIOR STATE: as left by feature 'resizer-docs'

REASON
Each widget returned by select(), radio(), checkbox(), datePicker(), slideSwitch() and
file() registered its own delegated listeners — twenty across the file — and discarded
every handle; select and datePicker additionally bound window scroll/resize and document
click listeners as anonymous closures. A page that rebuilt its form widgets therefore
accumulated listeners with no way to shed them.

Every attachEventHandler() call is now collected into the owning widget's eventHandles
array, the direct listeners in select and datePicker are named, and each widget's returned
body gained a destroy() that detaches everything it registered.

destroy() unbinds; it does not rebuild the page. These builders replace consumer markup in
place and never retain the original, so there is nothing to restore from. That is the
right scope for the case this exists to serve — a widget going away with the markup around
it — and pretending otherwise would mean silently reconstructing an element that is not
the one the consumer wrote.

